<Layout title="Privacy & Your Resume Data"><main id="main" class="content-page article"><h1>Your resume data</h1><p class="lead">This page explains how this version of GlobalCV handles the information you enter.</p><h2>Guest editing</h2><p>Your current resume is kept in your browser’s session storage to help it survive a reload and the sign-in flow. It is not a saved account draft. Browsers may restore sessions; use Start a new resume to clear the current editing session on a shared device.</p><h2>Document imports and downloads</h2><p>PDF, DOCX and TXT imports are processed in your browser. The original file is not uploaded. PDF downloads are generated in your browser. Imported text becomes part of your current editing session.</p><h2>Account drafts</h2><p>When you choose Save draft, your resume is sent to the draft service and associated with your authenticated account identifier. GlobalCV stores your name, email, a salted password hash and a hashed recovery code. Raw passwords and recovery codes are not stored. An HttpOnly session cookie keeps you logged in for up to seven days. Rate-limit records help prevent repeated login attempts. Your email identifies your account; email verification and email recovery are not provided in this version.</p><h2>Optional AI tailoring</h2><p>When you approve AI processing on Tailor my CV, GlobalCV sends the professional CV sections and job description to Groq. Your name and contact fields are excluded, but details you place in other sections are included. Remove sensitive information first. Groq does not use inputs or outputs for model training without permission; its service may retain them temporarily for reliability or abuse monitoring. See <a href="https://console.groq.com/docs/your-data" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Groq’s data policy</a>.</p><p>GlobalCV does not store the job description or AI suggestions on the server. They remain in the page until you leave; only an explicit Save as new draft stores the approved resume in your account. A daily usage counter uses a hashed account or network identifier and is removed after three days when the service is used. Guests sharing a network share their allowance. The limit resets at midnight UTC.</p><h2>Deleting a draft</h2><p>Use your dashboard to delete a saved resume. This removes it from the active draft database. Downloads already saved on your device remain under your control. Hosting-provider backup retention is separate from the active database.</p><h2>Third-party resources</h2><p>The site loads interface fonts from Google Fonts. The hosting provider process the network information needed to deliver and secure the service. AI processing occurs only with your approval in the tailoring feature. This version does not include advertising scripts or run session-recording analytics.</p><h2>Before advertising is enabled</h2><p>Advertising and any associated consent controls will require an updated disclosure. No active AdSense integration is included in this version.</p></main></Layout>
